  "texts": [
    "Why does a microwave heat food but leave the plate cold?",
    "Inside sits a magnetron, a tiny wave transmitter.",
    "It sends out microwaves that wiggle billions of times per second.",
    "And food is full of water.",
    "Water molecules behave like tiny magnets.",
    "Microwaves flip them back and forth.",
    "The molecules bump and rub against each other.",
    "Friction makes heat, like rubbing your hands together.",
    "Microwaves only reach a few centimeters into food.",
    "The rest spreads by conduction, so stir your food.",
    "The plate has almost no water, so it stays cooler.",
    "Metal reflects microwaves, that is why it sparks.",
    "The door has a metal mesh that keeps the waves inside.",
    "Its holes are smaller than the wave, but light gets through.",
    "Follow for more, and physics will never surprise you again!"
